From: prplMesh virtual-radio lab
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: resolve BSSID when association frame is unavailable

Open-source hostapd can emit AP-STA-CONNECTED without the raw association
request having first reached prplMesh. In that case the notification was
zero-initialized and forwarded with 00:00:00:00:00:00 as its BSSID. The
controller cannot attach the station to that non-existent BSS.

The hostapd event is delivered on the BSS control socket, so the resolved VAP
already identifies the authoritative BSSID. Use it as the fallback while
retaining the raw-frame BSSID and capability parsing whenever the frame is
available.

--- a/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
+++ b/common/beerocks/bwl/nl80211/ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp
@@ -1398,6 +1398,14 @@ bool ap_wlan_hal_nl80211::process_nl80211_event(parsed_obj_map_t &parsed_obj)
         if (m_latest_assoc_frame.find(src_mac) == m_latest_assoc_frame.end()) {
             LOG(WARNING) << "STA-CONNECTED without previously receiving a (re-)association frame!";
             msg->params.association_frame_length = 0;
+            auto vap = m_radio_info.available_vaps.find(vap_id);
+            if (vap == m_radio_info.available_vaps.end()) {
+                LOG(ERROR) << "No VAP information for connected STA on vap_id " << vap_id;
+                return false;
+            }
+            msg->params.bssid = tlvf::mac_from_string(vap->second.mac);
+            LOG(INFO) << "Resolved connected STA BSSID from VAP "
+                      << tlvf::mac_to_string(msg->params.bssid);
         } else {
             // Add the latest association frame
             // PPM-1718: parse the association frame and make sure it belongs to the right MAC address.
